# Proposed by the swarm (2026-10-14, F23); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: someone who comes from yabai ticks "Dock New Windows". From then on each window they open takes what is left over, or with
# nothing left half of the window they were working in. Small windows, windows of a fixed size and windows there is no room for float
# as they always did, and nothing ever turns into a tile because a window opened.
# Reference: T16 T18 T19 (inferred), Q13.
open Safari
expect floating 101
toggle-auto-dock
expect ok
# Windows that are open already stay as they are.
expect floating 101
dock 101 left
# Half of the screen is left over: the new window takes that, and Safari stays as it is.
open Notes
expect docked 102
expect still 101
expect left-of 101 102
# Nothing is left. The window being worked in is tall, so the next one goes below it.
open Terminal
expect docked 103
expect above 102 103
expect camera root
# An inspector and a calculator are not worth a place.
open Finder 265x520
expect floating 104
open Calculator 230x408 fixed
expect floating 105
expect count docked 3
# A window that insists on nearly the whole display fits nowhere, whatever room is made (F61). It floats, and nobody
# was squeezed to find that out.
focus 101
open Mail 1350x750 min 1300x700
expect floating 106
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
expect visible 103
expect count docked 3
close 104
close 105
close 106
# Looking at Notes and Terminal only: the new window joins them, and the view stays where it is.
cursor 1000 700
in
expect hidden 101
focus 102
# That half is wide, so the new one goes to its right.
open Music
expect docked 107
expect left-of 102 107
expect visible 103
expect hidden 101
# Framed on one window, a new one floats over it and stays with that view (F57).
zoom 101
open Preview
expect floating 108
expect camera 101
# Closing a window gives its room back.
show-all
close 107
expect count docked 3
# Off again: new windows float.
toggle-auto-dock
open Pages
expect floating 109
